= Project Objectives

This project aims to establish the fundations for an automated testbench for the smart collar. It should explore the state of the art in automated testing for embedded systems with hardware in the loop. It should also evaluate the most suitable testing framework between Pytest and Robot Framework, and implement a first version of the testbench on a development kit.

The architecture should be modular and scalable; it should be easy to add tests for new features and interfaces. It should be cost effective to be serialisable in a test farm. 

== Deliverables

- Mapping of testable collar interfaces and features: *@section:technical-context*
- Test strategies:  test cases, pass/fail criteria
- Evaluation report of Pytest vs Robot Framework for the testbench
- Initial testbench implemented on dev kit with modular and scalable architecture
- Functioning automated tests for BLE and power consumption
- Project report (this document)